\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{How we formulate finite acquisition evidence}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{acquisition}

\p{We formulate the family-level specialization as a demanding paired
comparison. The task family and evaluator are fixed independently, and both
protocols use the same inference budget. It is stronger than one acquisition
witness because the threshold change must hold for every member of #{G}.}

\p{A theorem may strengthen the witness with confidence bounds, transfer to a
predeclared related family, or a lower bound on newly successful support. Each
strengthening requires additional sampling or structural assumptions.}
